xpad version 1.0.2 README
-----------------------

xpad is a virtual sticky pad system for X using GTK+ 2.0.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALLATION NOTES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     To compile, just type "make" and / or "make install".

     Read the INSTALL file for more.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
USAGE NOTES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Right click to obtain configuration options and open new pads.
		You can also run xpad again to open a new pad.

     Closing a pad saves the contents for later.  Destroying one destroys
		the contents.

     Hold down CTRL and left-click drag to move a pad.  Hold down CTRL and 
		right-drag to resize a pad.

     Add xpad to your ~/.xinitrc to have xpad start with every X boot.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND ARGUMENTS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
	Standard GTK+ arguments are understood.  In addition, the following
		arguments are available.

	--help:			Prints usage information and exits.

	--version:		Prints version information and exits.

	--verbosity=%i: Where %i is the amount of output you desire.  0 is none;
					1 is moderate; 2 is debug.  Default is 0.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUGS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Font switching isn't perfect.  It does not auto-select your current font.
	I believe this to be a GTK+ problem.


